## 6. PERSISTENT INTERACTIVE TICKET PANEL

Create a permanent ticket panel that can be posted in a configured Discord channel.

It must remain functional after:

- Bot restarts.
- Server restarts.
- Deployments.
- Dashboard restarts.

The panel should be an elegant branded embed with a title such as:

**Silence Designs | Support Center**

Description:

"Welcome to Silence Designs Support. Select the appropriate option below to contact our team. Please provide accurate information so we can assist you efficiently."

Include a persistent dropdown menu with configurable categories:

- Place a Design Order.
- General Support.
- Report a Member.
- Report a Designer.
- Billing and Purchases.
- Partnerships.
- Advertisements.
- Other Inquiry.

When a customer chooses a category, create a ticket channel under the configured category and show the appropriate form.

### Order form

Use a Discord modal or a guided multi-step interaction to collect:

- Roblox username.
- Discord username, automatically populated where possible.
- Service type.
- What the customer wants.
- Description and specifications.
- Preferred colors.
- Text to include.
- Reference image URLs.
- Additional details.
- Preferred budget or pricing tier.

Discord modals have a limited number of input components and text-input sizes. If the form exceeds those limits, split it into multiple steps instead of creating an invalid modal.

Before final submission, show a review and confirmation step. Create the order record only after confirmation.

### Support form

For general support, do not force users to fill out an order questionnaire.

Ask:

- What do you need help with?
- Please describe your issue.
- Optional reference ID, purchase information, or screenshots.

Create the support ticket with the user's inquiry already displayed.

### Report form

Ask for:

- Person being reported.
- Their Discord ID or username, if known.
- Reason for the report.
- Supporting evidence or links.
- Additional context.

Make report tickets private and visible only to the reporting user and authorized support, administration, or management roles.

Do not reveal private reports to the reported person.

### Ticket embed

When a ticket opens, show a professional embed:

**Thanks for contacting support — @username**

"A member of our team will assist you shortly. Provide all relevant information regarding your issue. Kindly refrain from pinging agents while waiting for a response."

Include an Information section:

- Discord user and ID.
- Roblox username and profile link, when available.
- Roblox account creation/join information only when verified through a reliable source.
- Ticket category.
- Ticket reference ID.
- Creation time.

Include an Inquiry section containing the user's actual submitted question or request.

Use the following buttons:

- **Claim Ticket** — blue or neutral accent.
- **Close Ticket** — neutral or red accent.
- **Report** — red accent, for reporting an issue to the authorized team.

Only authorized support, administration, or management members may claim tickets. Enforce this server-side, not just by hiding buttons.

Ticket assignment must be exclusive unless management explicitly overrides it.

Staff must be able to add or remove users, transfer tickets, set priority, and generate transcripts.

### Ticket closure receipt

When a ticket is closed, generate a transcript and send a closure receipt to the ticket creator by DM when possible.

Use this format:

**Ticket Closure Receipt**

"Your support ticket was resolved and has now been closed."

"If you believe this ticket was closed in error or you need further assistance regarding the same issue, you may open a new ticket and include the Reference ID above so staff can quickly locate the previous conversation. Thank you for contacting us!"

Fields:

- Handler.
- Reference ID, such as `REF-B2EB6F7E`.
- Closure Reason.
- Closure date.
- Ticket category.

Generate unique reference IDs and store them permanently.

If DMs are disabled, log the delivery failure and retain the receipt and transcript for staff access.

